    "art": "One coherent ImageGen atlas with the original NW 16-cell motion guide and explorer Idle reference",
    "imagegen_prompt": "Image-to-image motion locked costume redraw. Image 1 is a square 4 by 4 walk animation atlas with sixteen registered cells. Render a NEW square atlas, EXACTLY the same sixteen positions in the same order, changing only character design to match Image 2. This is a single take of the same character and the same 2:1 rear-left northwest camera all the way around, including 15 to 00. Do not recenter any pose, restart the gait on a row boundary, improvise poses, make polished key poses by exaggeration, or move the ground contact position to suit the costume. The source's boots, knees, shoulder, hand, head silhouette position, body proportions, pelvis height, subtle head bob and exact orientations are the animation template. Treat the source like sixteen locked onion-skin drawing underlays. EACH heel, planted sole, lifted toe and hand stays where its counterpart is in that reference cell. Under the old cloak reconstruct the thighs between those original boots and the original pelvis. Body lengths and masses coherent. Use Image 2 only for appearance: short teal shoulder mantle and hood, curled brown hair, rolled beige cloth sleeves, thin wrist wraps, crossed brown straps, medium brown belt satchel in back, small rope coil, dark brown trousers and worn laced boots. Same painted texture and soft neutral lighting for every cell. Arms swing in subtle opposition with no resets.\nFrame progression to preserve: 00-02 small forward heel reach, the rear supporting boot slides progressively right-down in the in-place view; 03-05 gentle push-off with the other foot rising behind, then folding toward the body; 06-07 feet gather under the body with the swing boot LOW and gradually moving in front, no marching knees or leap; 08-10 low forward swing, smoothly extending the knee, opposite boot stays flat and moves slowly right-down; 11-14 front sole presses flat as the rear heel peels and the small backward leg gradually draws in, arms edge forward only gradually; 15-00 low passing and extension continues into the first frame with no pose jump. No third leg or swapped hands. No staccato resets. The image-one character centers, head heights and boot bounding positions must remain in the EXACT same relative locations in the sixteen equal square cells. Fill 75% of each cell height, same size across the atlas, keep margins and original camera/projection. True RGBA transparent background throughout. Leave out backdrop, floor shadow, numbers, boxes, marks and guides from input 1. One figure in each cell, exactly 4 rows and 4 columns.",
